})

body:
Users want to attach an agent run to a bug report.

- `GET /api/task/:taskId/export?format=json|markdown` (default `json`, auth like other task routes):
  - `json`: `{ task: <task detail>, metrics, events }` pretty-printed;
  - `markdown`: a readable transcript — title with issue number/title, a metrics summary (duration, LLM calls, tool calls, cost), then events grouped by step (`## Step N — <description>`), listing tool calls as bullet points (tool name + short args) and agent thoughts as blockquotes;
  - sets `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="task-<first 8 chars of id>.<json|md>"` and the right `Content-Type`;
  - `404` for unknown tasks, `400 { error }` for other formats.
- Put the formatting logic in a new `backend/src/services/taskExport.ts` (pure functions, easy to test) and add vitest tests for the markdown formatter.
- Frontend: `exportTaskLog(taskId, format)` in `frontend/src/api/client.ts` that downloads the file (fetch → blob → object URL → temporary `<a download>`), and a **Download log** control in `TaskView.tsx` offering JSON and Markdown.
- `npx tsc -b` must pass in backend and frontend.

`GithubApi.parseIssueUrl` is a naive string split: it accepts garbage, breaks on trailing slashes, query strings and `#fragments`, and silently treats pull-request URLs as issues. Fix it properly:

1. In `backend/src/GithubApi/index.ts`:
   - export `class InvalidIssueUrlError extends Error`;
   - `parseIssueUrl(url)` returns `{ host, owner, repo, issueNumber }` and accepts `https://github.com/o/r/issues/12`, with trailing slash, `?query`, `#fragment`, `www.github.com`, and any host listed in the comma-separated env `GITHUB_HOSTS` (GitHub Enterprise). It throws `InvalidIssueUrlError` for pull requests (`/pull/`), non-numeric or zero issue numbers, unknown hosts, `http://` URLs, and owner/repo names with characters GitHub doesn't allow;
   - the Octokit client uses `baseUrl: https://<host>/api/v3` for Enterprise hosts;
   - the clone URL in the orchestrator uses the parsed host.
2. `POST /api/task` and `POST /api/task/:taskId/retry` validate the URL first and return `400 { error: <message> }` for `InvalidIssueUrlError`; the stored task uses the normalized URL (`https://<host>/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<n>`).
3. Vitest tests in `backend/src/GithubApi/__tests__/parseIssueUrl.test.ts` covering at least 10 accepted/rejected cases.

`npx tsc -b` and `npm test` must pass in backend.
